{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSTyyXYDKPa6s76Pdzao","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — Shipment data class with `status: ShipmentStatus` field\n- `ShipmentStatus` enum at `Shipment.kt:23-27` with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED states\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — InMemoryShipmentRepository with `save()`, `findById()`, `existsById()` methods\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — POST `/shipments` (create), GET `/shipments/{id}` (read), GET `/shipments` (list)\n- `ErrorCode.kt:31-37` — Existing error codes: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:13-29` — Central error handling that converts ApiException to ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- All state-changing operations throw ApiException subclasses (ConflictException for 409, ResourceNotFoundException for 404)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler converts exceptions to consistent JSON envelope: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }`\n- Controllers return ResponseEntity with status codes or rely on exceptions for error paths\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions to verify both success and error responses\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ErrorCode.kt` — Must add error code for cancelled shipment case (cannot confirm a CANCELLED shipment)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must add `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests for the confirm endpoint\n\nAll these are within the shipment feature; no cross-module changes needed.\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotence: confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment must not fail (must return 200, not 409 or similar)\n- Thread safety: concurrent calls to confirm the same shipment (repository uses ConcurrentHashMap, should be safe)\n- Status transitions: only CREATED and CONFIRMED can confirm successfully; CANCELLED must fail with 409\n\n**Open questions:** None — the requirements are clear.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **ErrorCode.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code to the enum. This will be thrown when trying to confirm a CANCELLED shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint:\n   ```\n   POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Find the shipment by ID; if not found, throw ResourceNotFoundException with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE (409)\n   - If status is CREATED, update status to CONFIRMED, save, and return the updated shipment (200 OK)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing and return the shipment as-is (200 OK) — this ensures idempotence\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` — verifies CREATED → CONFIRMED transition and 200 response\n   - `confirms an already confirmed shipment idempotently` — verifies CONFIRMED state is unchanged and returns 200\n   - `rejects confirming a cancelled shipment with 409` — verifies CANCELLED shipments cannot be confirmed\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` — verifies 404 for missing shipment\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\nI considered using a service class to encapsulate the confirm logic, but the existing codebase has no service layer — the controller directly uses the repository. Adding a service layer would be architectural refactoring outside the scope of this ticket. The logic is simple enough to keep in the controller.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Logic | Output | HTTP |\n|------|-------|-------|--------|------|\n| Confirm CREATED | shipmentId='S-1', status=CREATED | Find shipment, set status=CONFIRMED, save | Updated shipment JSON | 200 |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED (idempotent) | shipmentId='S-1', status=CONFIRMED | Find shipment, status unchanged, return as-is | Shipment JSON (unchanged) | 200 |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | shipmentId='S-1', status=CANCELLED | Find shipment, throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE) | Error envelope with code | 409 |\n| Confirm non-existent | shipmentId='S-missing' | findById returns null, throw ResourceNotFoundException | Error envelope with code | 404 |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1 (created→confirmed): Create S-1, confirm it, assert status is CONFIRMED and response is 200\n- Test 2 (idempotent confirm): Create S-1, confirm it, confirm it again, assert status is still CONFIRMED and second confirm is 200\n- Test 3 (cancelled rejection): Manually insert CANCELLED shipment, attempt confirm, assert 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n- Test 4 (not found): Attempt to confirm non-existent S-missing, assert 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":977,"cache_read_input_tokens":17003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":977},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d40d1d49-9b5c-49b8-8b72-0b44e720e27a","uuid":"a6fcd2e4-daab-4c8f-95b1-9c31c0b38bea","timestamp":"2026-09-26T17:44:20.604Z","request_id":"req_011CfSTyxw4bo6RoQgmWks21"}
